From: Project Arctic
Subject: d3d11: H.264 video decoding on Vulkan Video.

ID3D11VideoDecoder for DXVA2 H264_VLD_NOFGT with short slice control, as
FFmpeg's d3d11va (scrcpy, mpv, browsers) and Media Foundation use it. The
picture parameters become an SPS and a PPS for the video session (the PPS
id, IDR and idr_pic_id from the first slice header), the reference frame
list a set of DPB slots on the layers of the decoder texture array, which
the video queue decodes into directly. Graphics signals a timeline
semaphore before each decode and waits for it after, so copies and draws
of the program stay in order with decoding without a CPU wait. Textures
made with D3D11_BIND_DECODER get the video profile, both queue families
and the GENERAL layout. Interlaced pictures (field, MBAFF) are refused.
---
